    "01. Core Concepts/Co-ordination Process": {
      "id": "01. Core Concepts/Co-ordination Process",
      "base_name": "Co-ordination Process",
      "rel_path": "01. Core Concepts/Co-ordination Process.md",
      "folder": "01. Core Concepts",
      "title": "Co-ordination process",
      "pillar": "Knowledge",
      "section": "Core Concepts",
      "subarea": "Management",
      "type": "process",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Co-ordination process\r\n\r\nCoordination in the **P",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Core Concepts]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Co-ordination process\r\n\r\nCoordination in the **Praxis Framework** is about enabling teams, suppliers, and stakeholders to move in a unified direction. It is practical, human-centered, and outcome-driven. In the words of a leadership mindset: we empower people to align purpose with delivery. And we build clarity so execution becomes a shared responsibility.\r\n\r\n## What Coordination Means\r\n\r\n* A continuous management activity\r\n* Ensures project, program, portfolio elements act in concert\r\n* Avoids duplication of effort, ambiguity, and operational silos\r\n* Drives timely decision-making and transparent communication\r\n\r\n> [!TIP] Coordination is woven into every Praxis function. It is not a separate role; it is a collective discipline.\r\n\r\n## Core Intent\r\n\r\n* Enhance alignment on objectives, priorities, and expectations\r\n* Strengthen integration across governance, delivery, and assurance\r\n* Build trust and accountability across all contributors\r\n* Enable agility and adaptability when change occurs\r\n\r\n## Where Coordination Operates\r\n\r\n* Across **lifecycle phases** from concept to closure\r\n* Between **delivery functions** such as scope, risk, schedule, finance\r\n* Within **governance structures** such as sponsorship and steering groups\r\n* Among **stakeholders** including customers, suppliers, communities\r\n\r\n## Pillars of Effective Coordination\r\n\r\n* **Clarity** of roles, interfaces, responsibilities\r\n* **Visibility** of information and performance indicators\r\n* **Cadence** of communication and collaboration rituals\r\n* **Consistency** in applying methods, standards, and controls\r\n* **Integration** of decisions and dependencies\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> Praxis treats coordination as a bridge between people, systems, and delivery practices.\r\n\r\n## Key Activities in Praxis Coordination\r\n\r\n* Aligning strategic objectives with delivery decisions\r\n* Managing interdependencies and handoffs\r\n* Resolving conflicts in priorities, resources, or timelines\r\n* Ensuring information flows to the right people at the right moment\r\n* Maintaining coherence between plans and realities on the ground\r\n* Supporting continuous review and adjustment\r\n\r\n## Collaboration and Stakeholder Engagement\r\n\r\n* Facilitate participation in planning and decision forums\r\n* Maintain stakeholder commitment throughout change\r\n* Surface concerns early and ensure feedback loops are active\r\n\r\n> [!TIP] Build a culture where coordination feels like empowerment, not policing.\r\n\r\n## Tools and Enablers\r\n\r\n* Integrated governance and reporting dashboards\r\n* Dependency mapping and interface management methods\r\n* Structured communications such as stand-ups, checkpoints, reviews\r\n* Common language for status, risk, and performance\r\n\r\n## Success Measures\r\n\r\n* Reduced friction in delivery processes\r\n* Increased predictability of outcomes\r\n* Faster resolution of dependencies and blockers\r\n* Stronger confidence across stakeholder groups\r\n\r\n## Leadership Mindset (channeling Satya Nadella)\r\n\r\n* Lead with empathy and transparency\r\n* Encourage partnership over hierarchy\r\n* Amplify every individual’s impact by connecting their work to the shared mission\r\n* Elevate innovation by making coordination a catalyst rather than a constraint\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n> Coordination in Praxis is about creating coherence without sacrificing agility.\r\n\r\n## Closing Thought\r\n\r\nWhen coordination is done well, teams don’t feel controlled; they feel empowered. They understand how their work contributes to something larger. And the organization gains velocity with purpose.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Core Concepts Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Closure Process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Complexity]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
    },
