      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Definition Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Definition Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The life cycle process where the project or programme is planned in full detail, producing management plans, delivery plans, and the full business case.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Definition Process** takes the approved [[Brief]] and elaborates it into a fully articulated, integrated baseline for execution. It answers *what* will be delivered, *how* it will be governed, *when* it will happen, and *how much* it will cost.\r\n\r\n## Key Activities\r\n1. **Assemble Management Plans**: Author policies and procedures for Risk, Quality, Scope, Schedule, Finance, Resources, Stakeholders, and Change.\r\n2. **Develop Solution & Specifications**: Engineer technical architectures and detailed product breakdowns.\r\n3. **Prepare Delivery Plans**: Schedule stages/tranches, estimate costs, and balance resources.\r\n4. **Finalize Business Case**: Complete comprehensive investment appraisal and benefits forecasts.\r\n5. **Gateway Review (Gate 2)**: Sponsor and governing body authorize entry into delivery.\r\n\r\n## Key Outputs\r\n- Full [[Manage The Business Case|Business Case]].\r\n- All functional [[Management Plans]].\r\n- Master [[Delivery Plan]] and first Stage Plan.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Context]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Delivery Process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
