      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Development Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Delivery Process]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Development Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The technical life cycle process responsible for engineering, testing, and constructing the project's deliverables.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Development Process** (or Solutions Development) runs in parallel with the [[Delivery Process]]. While the Delivery Process handles project governance and management, the Development Process focuses on the technical creation and engineering of the outputs.\r\n\r\n## Core Activities\r\n1. **Requirements Analysis**: Elaborating user stories, technical requirements, and acceptance criteria.\r\n2. **Design & Architecture**: Engineering functional and physical architectures.\r\n3. **Construction & Assembly**: Coding, fabrication, configuration, or authoring.\r\n4. **Testing & Integration**: Verifying deliverables against specifications and quality criteria.\r\n5. **Deployment & Handover**: Commissioning deliverables into the operational environment.\r\n\r\n## Relationship to Praxis Method\r\nThe Development Process is typically domain-specific (e.g., Agile software development, waterfall engineering, construction protocols) and interfaces seamlessly with the managerial [[Delivery Process]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Delivery Process Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Environment]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
