      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Governance]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Governance Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The overarching framework of decision-making, authority limits, stakeholder accountability, and oversight governing all P3 activities.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Governance Process** provides the structural mechanisms, controls, and oversight necessary to ensure projects, programmes, and portfolios achieve their objectives ethically, legally, and efficiently.\r\n\r\n## Principles\r\n- **Separation of Direction and Management**: Clear distinction between the Sponsor (direction/ownership) and the Project Manager (day-to-day management).\r\n- **Tolerances & Escalation**: Autonomous operation within agreed boundaries; mandatory escalation when boundaries are threatened.\r\n- **Stage / Tranche Gateways**: Formal approval gates before committing resources to successive phases.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee [[Governance]], [[Assurance]], and [[Sponsorship Process]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Governance Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Environment]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Identification Process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
