      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Identification Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Identification Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The initial life cycle process that develops an outline of the project or programme to assess viability before committing major definition investment.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Identification Process** is triggered by a [[Mandate]]. Its primary purpose is to establish an initial outline of the project or programme, determine whether it is worthwhile, and secure sponsor commitment to fund the [[Definition Process]].\r\n\r\n## Key Activities\r\n1. **Appoint Sponsor & Project Manager**: Establish core initial leadership.\r\n2. **Develop Brief**: Capture background, objectives, initial scope, and high-level business justification.\r\n3. **Draft Outline Business Case**: Preliminary investment appraisal.\r\n4. **Prepare Definition Plan**: Detailed schedule and budget for running the definition phase.\r\n5. **Authorise Definition**: Sponsor formal gateway review to approve or reject further work.\r\n\r\n## Key Inputs & Outputs\r\n- **Inputs**: Strategic Mandate, Lessons Log from past projects.\r\n- **Outputs**: Project/Programme [[Brief]], Outline Business Case, [[Definition Plan]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Governance Process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Initiation Process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
