      "title": "Initiation Process",
      "pillar": "Method",
      "section": "Portfolio Processes",
      "subarea": "Process",
      "type": "process",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Initiation Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Initiation Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The portfolio management process that establishes the portfolio's governance infrastructure, strategic scope, and operating model.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Initiation Process** sets up a new portfolio or realigns an existing one with corporate strategy. It establishes the organizational structure, resources, and governance rules required to direct projects and programmes consistently.\r\n\r\n## Key Activities\r\n1. **Define Portfolio Scope**: Determine which organizational domains, investments, and programmes fall within the portfolio boundary.\r\n2. **Establish Governance Infrastructure**: Setup PMO / support functions, reporting channels, and resource pools.\r\n3. **Draft Portfolio Management Plans**: Tailor framework policies for risk, scheduling, and finance across all components.\r\n4. **Secure Executive Endorsement**: Board sign-off on the portfolio charter.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nConnects to [[Co-ordinate A Portfolio]], [[Categorisation Process]], and [[Prioritisation Process]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Identification Process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Integrative Management]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
