      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Overview of Identification Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> High-level summary of the first phase of the project and programme life cycle.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Overview of Identification Process** summarizes the initial gateway where ideas and mandates are transformed into justifiable project briefs.\r\n\r\n## Key Goals\r\n- Rapidly determine if the proposed work is viable and aligned with strategy.\r\n- Prevent premature commitment of extensive organizational resources.\r\n- Produce the [[Brief]] and [[Definition Plan]] for Sponsor authorization.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee full details in [[Identification Process]] and [[Identify A Project Or Programme]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Overview of Contract management]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Portfolio Process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
