      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Prioritisation Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Prioritisation Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Evaluates candidate projects and programmes against strategic objectives to rank them in order of value, urgency, and resource feasibility.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Prioritisation Process** evaluates potential and active components within a portfolio to determine their relative rank and strategic priority.\r\n\r\n## Key Activities\r\n1. **Define Scoring Criteria**: Establish weighted strategic metrics (ROI, strategic fit, risk profile, regulatory compliance).\r\n2. **Score & Rank Initiatives**: Assess candidate business cases against the criteria.\r\n3. **Balance Resource Constraints**: Identify bottlenecks in capital, skilled talent, or supply chain.\r\n4. **Recommend Portfolio Composition**: Present prioritized options to the executive portfolio board.\r\n\r\n## Outputs\r\n- Prioritized project and programme pipeline.\r\n- Portfolio investment recommendations.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Portfolio Process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
