      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n Sponsorship Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Pro",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Governance]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `process`\r\n\r\n# Sponsorship Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Provides senior executive ownership, strategic alignment, resource authorization, and benefit advocacy across the life cycle.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Sponsorship Process** defines the executive role that links the project or programme to the strategic leadership of the host organization. The Sponsor is the ultimate owner of the [[Business Case]].\r\n\r\n## Key Responsibilities\r\n- Champion the vision and secure funding.\r\n- Authorize project initiation, stage boundaries, and closure.\r\n- Set management tolerances for cost, time, and scope.\r\n- Resolve escalated issues from the project manager.\r\n- Ensure organizational change is realized to deliver benefits.\r\n\r\n## Relationships\r\nConnects to [[Sponsorship]] and [[Sponsor A Project Or Programme]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Governance Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Setting]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
