      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Processes`\r\n\r\n Processes\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> The life cycle ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Processes`\r\n\r\n# Processes\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> The life cycle process model for projects, programmes, and portfolios, from initiation to closure.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (11)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Context of Governance process]] | `Process` | Governance does not float in the ether. It is not an abstract set of rules imposed upon a vacuum. It exists within a nes |\r\n| [[Deliver a Project or Programme Competency]] | `Process` | - The purpose of this competency is to demonstrate the ability to achieve the goals of the **delivery process**. This pr |\r\n| [[Goal of Closure process]] | `Concept` | Core goals, handover criteria, and success metrics for closing a project or programme. |\r\n| [[Goal of Sponsorship process]] | `Concept` | Strategic aims, executive ownership, and governance gateways operated by the project sponsor. |\r\n| [[Goal of Support]] | `Concept` | The goals and scope of project, programme, and portfolio support offices (PMO). |\r\n| [[Goals of Definition process]] | `Concept` | Detailed objectives and success criteria for the definition planning phase. |\r\n| [[Lead]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the ability to inspire, guide, and motivate teams and stakeholders to achieve common project objectives. |\r\n| [[Overall Goal of Management process]] | `Concept` | The overarching objectives of day-to-day project and programme management. |\r\n| [[Overview of Co-ordination process]] | `Process` | Summary of portfolio-wide coordination, interdependency management, and resource balancing. |\r\n| [[Project & Programme Management]] | `Process` | - The Praxis method provides a **single, generic process model** for managing both projects and programmes. |\r\n| [[Purpose of Change management plan]] | `Concept` | Explains the purpose, scope, and principles of the Change Management Plan. | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
