      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n Goal of Closure Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n>",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Goal of Closure Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Core goals, handover criteria, and success metrics for closing a project or programme.\r\n\r\n## Goals of the Closure Process\r\nThe primary goals of the **Closure Process** in the Praxis Framework are:\r\n1. **Deliverable Handover**: Formally transfer ownership of outputs and products to the operational teams or client.\r\n2. **Performance Review**: Evaluate project performance against the approved business case, delivery plans, and baseline tolerances.\r\n3. **Capture Lessons**: Record institutional insights, successes, and learning in the [[Lessons Log]].\r\n4. **Demobilise Resources**: Orderly release of personnel, facilities, and physical assets back to the organization.\r\n5. **Contractual & Financial Close**: Finalize supplier accounts, release retentions, and archive records.\r\n\r\n## Related Documents\r\n- [[Follow-on Actions Report]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n- [[Close a project or programme]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Deliver a Project or Programme Competency]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Goal of Sponsorship process]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
