    "03. Processes/Goal of Sponsorship process": {
      "id": "03. Processes/Goal of Sponsorship process",
      "base_name": "Goal of Sponsorship process",
      "rel_path": "03. Processes/Goal of Sponsorship process.md",
      "folder": "03. Processes",
      "title": "Goal of Sponsorship Process",
      "pillar": "Method",
      "section": "Governance",
      "subarea": "Process",
      "type": "concept",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n Goal of Sponsorship Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overvie",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Governance]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Goal of Sponsorship Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Strategic aims, executive ownership, and governance gateways operated by the project sponsor.\r\n\r\n## Goals of the Sponsorship Process\r\nThe sponsorship process connects executive strategy with project execution. Its primary goals are to:\r\n1. **Provide Executive Direction**: Maintain ongoing alignment between the project and corporate strategy.\r\n2. **Own the Business Case**: Ensure that investment expenditure remains justified by expected benefits.\r\n3. **Authorize Gateway Transitions**: Authorize entry into Definition, Delivery, and Closure phases.\r\n4. **Establish Tolerances**: Define managerial boundaries for cost, schedule, risk, and scope.\r\n5. **Resolve Escalations**: Adjudicate issues exceeding the project manager's delegated authority.\r\n\r\n## Related Concepts\r\n- [[Sponsorship]]\r\n- [[Sponsor A Project Or Programme]]\r\n- [[Governance Process]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Governance Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Goal of Closure process]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Goal of Support]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
    },
