      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n Goals of Definition Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overvie",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Goals of Definition Process\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Detailed objectives and success criteria for the definition planning phase.\r\n\r\n## Goals of the Definition Process\r\nThe **Definition Process** establishes the baselines for the entire project or programme. Its primary goals are:\r\n1. **Define Scope & Solutions**: Translate user requirements into technical specifications and work breakdown structures.\r\n2. **Assemble Functional Policies**: Author comprehensive [[Management Plans]] for risk, schedule, finance, and quality.\r\n3. **Build Integrated Delivery Plans**: Formulate resource-balanced schedules and budgets for delivery stages.\r\n4. **Justify the Investment**: Produce a robust, defensible [[Business Case]] with realistic ROI.\r\n5. **Obtain Commitment**: Secure formal sponsor approval and governance sign-off to start execution.\r\n\r\n## Related Notes\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Plan]]\r\n- [[Define A Project Or Programme]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Project and Programme Processes Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Goal of Support]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Lead]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[Identification Process]]\r\n- [[Definition Process]]\r\n- [[Delivery Process]]\r\n- [[Closure Process]]\r\n"
