      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n Purpose of Change Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] O",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Purpose of Change Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Explains the purpose, scope, and principles of the Change Management Plan.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Change Management Plan** documents the strategy for managing the organizational and human transformation required to adopt project deliverables and achieve desired business benefits.\r\n\r\n## Distinction in Praxis\r\n- **Scope Change Control**: Handled by [[Control Scope Change]] and [[General Principles of Configuration Management]] to protect product baselines.\r\n- **Organizational Change Management**: Handled by the Change Management Plan to transition business teams, adjust culture, and embed new workflows.\r\n\r\n## Key Contents\r\n- Stakeholder impact assessments and readiness surveys.\r\n- Training curricula and transition schedules.\r\n- Change agent networks and operational support mechanisms.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee [[Manage Change]], [[Goal of Change Management]], and [[Change control]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Project & Programme Management]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
