      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Change Management`\r\n\r\n# Change Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Change Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (7)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Change control]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Change control is the formal process by which all requests to change a baselined scope are captured, e |\r\n| [[Change management Artefact]] | `Artefact` | The structured document setting out organizational change policy, procedures, and transition plans. |\r\n| [[Change Management Capability Maturity]] | `Maturity` | - The function of Change Management should: |\r\n| [[Change management]] | `Concept` | The management function that guides individuals and teams through organizational transitions to realize benefits. |\r\n| [[Control Scope Change]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to capture change requests, evaluate impacts, and obtain authorized decisions before changin |\r\n| [[Goal of Change Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: The achievement of benefits in a business case often requires changes to the working practices of the  |\r\n| [[Manage Change]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to plan, lead, and embed organizational and cultural transitions required to realize busines | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
