      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n Change Management Artefact\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overvie",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n# Change Management Artefact\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The structured document setting out organizational change policy, procedures, and transition plans.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nThe **Change Management Artefact** (Change Management Plan) defines the approach to facilitating organizational adoption of project deliverables.\r\n\r\n## Structure\r\n- **Change Vision**: The desired future operational state.\r\n- **Readiness Assessment**: Evaluation of stakeholder willingness and capability to change.\r\n- **Intervention Plan**: Communications, coaching, training, and incentive programs.\r\n- **Benefits Alignment**: Verification that organizational changes yield the planned business benefits.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee [[Purpose of Change management plan]], [[Manage Change]], and [[Change Management Capability Maturity]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Change management]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Change Management Capability Maturity]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
