      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Change Management\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The management function that guides individuals and teams through organizational transitions to realize benefits.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n**Change Management** is the discipline that guides how we prepare, equip, and support individuals to successfully adopt change in order to drive organizational success and outcomes.\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n1. Identify the organizational and cultural changes required to convert outputs into benefits.\r\n2. Prepare the host business through engagement, leadership, and training.\r\n3. Embed new practices into business-as-usual operations.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee [[Goal of Change Management]], [[Manage Change]], and [[Change control]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Change Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Change control]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Change management Artefact]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
