      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Communication Management`\r\n\r\n# Communication Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Communication Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (7)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Communicate]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to transmit clear, concise, and compelling messages across varied media and audiences. |\r\n| [[Communication Plan]] | `Artefact` | A schedule and strategy specifying what messages will be communicated to which stakeholders, through what media, and at  |\r\n| [[Communication]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Communication is the means by which information is exchanged and a common understanding is achieved be |\r\n| [[General Principles of Information Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Information management is the collection, storage, dissemination, archiving, and eventual destruction  |\r\n| [[Information Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Governs how project data, records, documentation, and institutional knowledge are captured, stored, secured, and distrib |\r\n| [[Information Management]] | `Maturity` | Capability maturity benchmarks and assessment criteria for organizational information management. |\r\n| [[Manage Information]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to establish information governance, document control, and record archiving. | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
