      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Procurement Management`\r\n\r\n Procurement Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Sectio",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Procurement Management`\r\n\r\n# Procurement Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Procurement Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (3)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Contract Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Contract management includes the negotiation, creation, and ongoing administration of a legally bindin |\r\n| [[Manage Contracts]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to administer, monitor, and enforce legal and commercial agreements with suppliers. |\r\n| [[Procurement]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Procurement covers the acquisition from a supplier of the products and services required for the compl | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
