      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Resource Management`\r\n\r\n# Resource Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Resource Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (7)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[General Principles of Resource Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Resource management covers all aspects of the planning, acquisition, deployment, and control of the re |\r\n| [[Manage Resources]] | `Concept` | - The purpose of this competency is to demonstrate the ability to achieve the goals of resource management. These goals  |\r\n| [[Mobilise Resources]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to onboard, organize, and equip personnel, facilities, and equipment for project execution. |\r\n| [[Procure Resources]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to specify requirements, evaluate vendors, and establish commercial supply contracts. |\r\n| [[Resource Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Defines how internal and external resources (people, equipment, materials, facilities) will be acquired, scheduled, and  |\r\n| [[Resource Management]] | `Maturity` | Capability maturity attributes for securing, scheduling, and managing physical and human resources. |\r\n| [[Resource Scheduling]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Resource scheduling is a collection of techniques used to analyse the resources required to deliver th | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
