      "title": "Resource Management Plan",
      "pillar": "Method",
      "section": "Resource Management",
      "subarea": "Documentation",
      "type": "artefact",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n Resource Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Resource Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n# Resource Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Defines how internal and external resources (people, equipment, materials, facilities) will be acquired, scheduled, and managed.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Resource Management Plan** provides the strategy for securing and managing the physical, technical, and human assets required to deliver the work.\r\n\r\n## Structure\r\n- **Resource Identification**: Skills matrix, capacity planning, equipment requirements.\r\n- **Procurement Strategy**: Internal resource allocation vs. external contract engagement.\r\n- **Mobilisation & Demobilisation**: Handover schedules and release dates.\r\n- **Resource Smoothing & Levelling**: Guidelines for resolving resource over-allocation.\r\n\r\n## Relationships\r\nMaps directly to [[General Principles of Resource Management]] and [[Resource Scheduling]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Resource Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Resource Management]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Resource Scheduling]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
