      "type": "maturity",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Capability Maturity | **Type**: `maturity`\r\n\r\n Resource Management Maturity\r\n\r\n> [!S",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Resource Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Capability Maturity | **Type**: `maturity`\r\n\r\n# Resource Management Maturity\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Capability maturity attributes for securing, scheduling, and managing physical and human resources.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nDefines the maturity benchmarks for **Resource Management** across projects, programmes, and portfolios.\r\n\r\n## Capability Attributes\r\n- **Level 1**: Localized, reactive resource allocation; constant resource conflicts between departments.\r\n- **Level 2**: Formal [[Resource Management Plan]] applied; stage-based resource schedules and procurement procedures.\r\n- **Level 3**: Centralized resource management system; enterprise skills inventories and multi-project leveling.\r\n- **Level 4**: Quantitative capacity planning, utilization metrics, and predictive supplier performance modeling.\r\n- **Level 5**: Dynamic resource allocation responding to strategic shifts; proactive workforce capability development.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nConnects to [[General Principles of Resource Management]], [[Resource Scheduling]], and [[Resource Management Capability Maturity]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Resource Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Procure Resources]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Resource Management Plan]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
