      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Risk Management`\r\n\r\n Risk Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Risk Management`\r\n\r\n# Risk Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Risk Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (7)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[General Principles of Risk Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Risk management is the function that allows individual risk events and overall risk to be understood a |\r\n| [[Manage Risk]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to identify, assess, plan responses for, and monitor risks across the life cycle. |\r\n| [[Risk Management Capability Maturity]] | `Maturity` | - The function of Risk Management should: |\r\n| [[Risk Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | The Risk Management Plan sets out how risk management will be conducted across the project, programme, or portfolio. |\r\n| [[Risk Management]] | `Maturity` | Organizational capability maturity benchmarks for proactive risk management. |\r\n| [[Risk Register]] | `Artefact` | The Risk Register is a living delivery document that records and tracks all identified risk events, assessments, and res |\r\n| [[Risk Techniques]] | `Concept` | - Risk techniques are the specific tools and methods used within the **identification**, **assessment**, and **response  | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
