      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Schedule Management`\r\n\r\n# Schedule Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Schedule Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (5)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[General Principles of Schedule Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: A schedule is a timetable showing the work involved in a project, programme, or portfolio. It is a dyn |\r\n| [[Manage The Schedule]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to plan, develop, optimize, and control project time schedules. |\r\n| [[Schedule Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Establishes the criteria, tools, and methodologies for developing, maintaining, and controlling project schedules. |\r\n| [[Schedule Management]] | `Management-area` | - The function of Schedule Management should: |\r\n| [[Time Scheduling]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Time scheduling techniques are used to develop and present schedules that show **when** work will be p | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
