      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Scope Management`\r\n\r\n Scope Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Scope Management`\r\n\r\n# Scope Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Scope Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (5)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Manage Scope]] | `Concept` | - The purpose of this competency is to demonstrate the ability to achieve the goals of scope management. These goals are |\r\n| [[Overall Goal of Scope Management]] | `Management-area` | - The function of Scope Management should: |\r\n| [[Scope Document]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Scope documents are the collection of documents that collectively describe the **objectives of the wor |\r\n| [[Scope Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Defines how scope will be captured, verified, structured into a WBS/PBS, and protected against unauthorized scope creep. |\r\n| [[Scope Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Scope management is the function that identifies, defines, and controls the objectives of the work, in | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
