      "pillar": "Method",
      "section": "Scope Management",
      "subarea": "Documentation",
      "type": "artefact",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n Scope Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> ",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Scope Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n# Scope Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Defines how scope will be captured, verified, structured into a WBS/PBS, and protected against unauthorized scope creep.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Scope Management Plan** defines the process for determining, validating, and controlling the work and deliverables of the initiative.\r\n\r\n## Contents\r\n- **Requirements Engineering**: Techniques for elicitation, prioritisation (MoSCoW), and validation.\r\n- **Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)**: Standards for creating deliverable-oriented breakdown structures.\r\n- **Scope Verification & Acceptance**: Formal procedures for deliverable inspection and sign-off.\r\n- **Scope Baseline & Control**: Integration with change control procedures.\r\n\r\n## Relationships\r\nGoverns the [[Scope Management]] area and [[Product Documents]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Scope Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Scope Management]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
