      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `Stakeholder Management`\r\n\r\n# Stakeholder Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Comprehensive guide to Stakeholder Management covering principles, management plans, registers, competencies, and capability maturity.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (5)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[General Principles of Stakeholder Management]] | `Management-area` | - **Definition**: Stakeholder management is the function that ensures stakeholders are appropriately identified, underst |\r\n| [[Manage Stakeholders]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to identify stakeholders, analyze interests and influence, and execute engagement plans. |\r\n| [[Stakeholder Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | The Stakeholder Management Plan defines how stakeholders will be identified, analyzed, and engaged throughout the life c |\r\n| [[Stakeholder Management]] | `Maturity` | Maturity benchmarks for identifying, analyzing, and engaging stakeholders. |\r\n| [[Stakeholder Register]] | `Artefact` | The Stakeholder Register documents all stakeholders, their interests, influence levels, and tailored engagement approach | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
