      "type": "concept",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n Solution Architecture\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Solutions Development]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Type**: `concept`\r\n\r\n# Solution Architecture\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> The practice of designing comprehensive technical and operational solutions that fulfill the project scope and specifications.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n**Solution Architecture** translates business requirements into viable, scalable, and resilient technical or operational models. It bridges the gap between the business problem and the engineering implementation.\r\n\r\n## Key Objectives\r\n- Ensure alignment between technical designs and the [[Business Case]].\r\n- Evaluate trade-offs between cost, time, complexity, and technical debt.\r\n- Define interfaces, data flows, and architectural constraints.\r\n- Verify feasibility through prototypes and proof-of-concepts during the [[Definition Process]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Solutions Development Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Process Competencies]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Teamwork]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
