      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Documentation & Artefacts`\r\n\r\n# Documentation & Artefacts\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Management plans, scope documents, registers, and delivery reports supporting life cycle governance.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (25)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Business case management]] | `Artefact` | - **Definition**: Business case management is the function concerned with developing, communicating, and maintaining the |\r\n| [[Configuration Management]] | `Artefact` | Outlines how assets, deliverables, and documents are identified, version-controlled, tracked, and audited. |\r\n| [[Control Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Defines the policies, reporting cadences, tolerances, and escalation procedures for tracking and controlling delivery pe |\r\n| [[Daily Log]] | `Artefact` | An informal diary maintained by the project or programme manager to record daily events, ideas, minor issues, and remind |\r\n| [[Definition Plan]] | `Artefact` | A delivery plan created in the identification process describing how the definition phase will be conducted, resourced,  |\r\n| [[Delivery Documents]] | `Artefact` | - **Role and Purpose**: While management plans set out the governance principles (\"how to manage\") and scope documents d |\r\n| [[Delivery Plan]] | `Artefact` | A comprehensive operational plan detailing the work, schedule, budget, and resources for a specific stage or tranche. |\r\n| [[Documentation]] | `Artefact` | - In the Praxis Framework, P3 management documents are organised into three main categories. This structure helps to cla |\r\n| [[Finance Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Sets out the policy and procedures for budgeting, cash flow forecasting, accounting, and financial control. |\r\n| [[Follow-on Actions Report]] | `Artefact` | Documents unresolved issues, ongoing maintenance responsibilities, and residual risks transferred to operational teams u |\r\n| [[General Principles of Configuration Management]] | `Artefact` | - **Definition**: Configuration management encompasses the administrative activities concerned with the creation, mainte |\r\n| [[General Principles of Requirements Management]] | `Artefact` | - **Definition**: Requirements management is the function that establishes stakeholders’ wants and needs, and then revie |\r\n| [[Issue Register]] | `Artefact` | The Issue Register records all problems, deviations, and unforeseen events that exceed local tolerance and require forma |\r\n| [[Lessons Log]] | `Artefact` | The Lessons Log captures knowledge and experience gained during the project or programme to improve current and future p |\r\n| [[Manage Requirements]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to capture, document, prioritize, and baseline user and technical requirements. |\r\n| [[Manage The Business Case]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to formulate, justify, maintain, and confirm the viability of the project business case. |\r\n| [[Manage The Configuration]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to maintain product integrity through identification, status accounting, and verification au |\r\n| [[Manage The Organisation]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to structure project governance, define managerial roles, and maintain team cohesion. |\r\n| [[Management Plans]] | `Artefact` | - **Definition**: Management plans are a category of **governance documents**. They set out the way a specific function  |\r\n| [[Organisation Management Plan]] | `Artefact` | Outlines the structure, roles, responsibilities, reporting lines, and appointment processes for the P3 management team. |\r\n| [[Product Documents]] | `Artefact` | A collection of granular specifications, descriptions, and quality criteria for individual products and components. |\r\n| [[Progress Report]] | `Artefact` | A periodic, time-driven report from the project or programme manager to the sponsor and governing body summarizing perfo |\r\n| [[Requirements Management]] | `Maturity` | Capability maturity benchmarks for eliciting, structuring, and baselining scope requirements. |\r\n| [[Support]] | `Artefact` | - **Definition**: Support is a set of specialist and administrative services carried out on behalf of project, programme |\r\n| [[Uncertainty And Agility]] | `Artefact` | - The concept of agility in project delivery has its roots in the idea of **VUCA**. | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
