      "type": "artefact",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n Finance Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Financial Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n# Finance Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Sets out the policy and procedures for budgeting, cash flow forecasting, accounting, and financial control.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Finance Management Plan** describes how the financial resources of the project or programme will be budgeted, secured, tracked, and audited throughout the life cycle.\r\n\r\n## Core Elements\r\n- **Cost Categorization**: Capital expenditure (CapEx) vs. Operational expenditure (OpEx), direct vs. indirect costs.\r\n- **Estimating Standards**: Bottom-up, parametric, or analogous estimation methodologies.\r\n- **Contingency & Reserves**: Management reserves and contingency funds allocation rules.\r\n- **Financial Controls**: Sign-off limits, invoice approval workflows, and audit requirements.\r\n\r\n## Life Cycle Timing\r\nAuthored during the [[Definition Process]] and executed in [[Budgeting and cost control]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Financial Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Documentation]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Follow-on Actions Report]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
