      "title": "Organisation Management Plan",
      "pillar": "Method",
      "section": "Organisation Management",
      "subarea": "Documentation",
      "type": "artefact",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n Organisation Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overv",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Organisation Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Type**: `artefact`\r\n\r\n# Organisation Management Plan\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Outlines the structure, roles, responsibilities, reporting lines, and appointment processes for the P3 management team.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Organisation Management Plan** establishes the temporary governance structure needed to manage and direct the project, programme, or portfolio.\r\n\r\n## Key Sections\r\n- **Governance Hierarchy**: Sponsor, Programme/Project Board, Management Team, Team Managers.\r\n- **Role Descriptions**: Detailed terms of reference for all managerial appointments.\r\n- **Staffing & Recruitment**: How human resources are onboarded, inducted, and released.\r\n- **Decision Authority**: Delegated limits of authority and escalation pathways.\r\n\r\n## Timing\r\nCreated in the [[Definition Process]] by the Project/Programme Manager.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Organisation Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Management Plans]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Product Documents]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
