      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Portfolio Management`\r\n\r\n# Portfolio Management\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Strategic portfolio initiation, categorisation, prioritisation, balancing, coordination, and community of practice.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (11)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Co-ordinate A Portfolio]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to coordinate concurrent projects and programmes, balancing interdependencies and resource p |\r\n| [[Communities Of Practice]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Communities of Practice (CoPs) are groups of people who share a common interest in P3 management or a  |\r\n| [[Initiate A Portfolio]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to design portfolio governance, establish operating models, and define portfolio boundaries. |\r\n| [[Manage A Portfolio]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to direct and govern a portfolio across categorisation, prioritisation, and performance cycl |\r\n| [[Manage Boundaries]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to govern stage and tranche transitions, conducting gateway reviews and evaluating ongoing v |\r\n| [[Manage The Finance]] | `Concept` | - The purpose of this competency is to demonstrate the ability to achieve the goals of financial management. These goals |\r\n| [[Project, Programme And Portfolio Management]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Project, Programme, and Portfolio Management (P3M) is the application of methods, procedures, techniqu |\r\n| [[Projects, Programmes And Portfolios]] | `Concept` | - The terms **Project, Programme, and Portfolio (P3)** are used to describe typical combinations of complexity and envir |\r\n| [[Specification]] | `Artefact` | Defines the tangible and intangible outputs to be produced, detailing technical, functional, and quality requirements. |\r\n| [[Sustainability]] | `Concept` | - Sustainability is a concept of increasing importance in all aspects of business and society. |\r\n| [[Vision Statement]] | `Artefact` | A concise, inspirational declaration of the future state that the project or programme aims to deliver. | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
