      "subarea": "Management Competencies",
      "type": "competency",
      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Competence | **Type**: `competency`\r\n\r\n Co-ordinate A Portfolio Competency\r\n\r\n> [!SU",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Competence | **Type**: `competency`\r\n\r\n# Co-ordinate A Portfolio Competency\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Demonstrates the capability to coordinate concurrent projects and programmes, balancing interdependencies and resource pools.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Co-ordinate A Portfolio** competency certifies a portfolio manager's ability to maintain cross-initiative balance, resolve competing priorities, and align shared delivery milestones.\r\n\r\n## Performance Criteria\r\n1. Monitor interdependencies between projects and programmes within the portfolio.\r\n2. Resolve multi-project resource conflicts and prioritize allocations.\r\n3. Coordinate portfolio-level risk responses and contingency reserves.\r\n4. Maintain aggregate reporting dashboards for executive leadership.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Portfolio Management Overview]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Communities Of Practice]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
