      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Delivery & Lifecycle`\r\n\r\n Delivery & Lifecycle\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overv",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Method | **Section**: `Delivery & Lifecycle`\r\n\r\n# Delivery & Lifecycle\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Operational delivery, work package control, mobilisation, solutions engineering, and team execution.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (15)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Close a project or programme]] | `Process` | The structured process for demobilising teams, handing over deliverables, capturing lessons, and archiving records. |\r\n| [[Conflict Management]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Conflict is typically perceived as something negative that has a detrimental impact on achieving objec |\r\n| [[Define A Project Or Programme]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to execute the definition process, producing management plans, schedules, and the full busin |\r\n| [[Deliver A Project Or Programme]] | `Process` | The operational execution process where work packages are managed and controlled. |\r\n| [[Delivery Process Maturity]] | `Process` | - The goals of this process are to: |\r\n| [[Delivery]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: The \"Delivery\" area of P3 management is about the core functions that are immediately and directly con |\r\n| [[Develop Products]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to execute technical work packages to build and verify required outputs. |\r\n| [[Develop Solution]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to evaluate alternative technical options and design optimal deliverable solutions. |\r\n| [[Identify A Project Or Programme]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to transform mandates into project briefs and evaluate preliminary viability. |\r\n| [[Mobilisation]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Mobilisation is the function that ensures the appropriate organisational and technical infrastructures |\r\n| [[Overview of Mobilisation]] | `Concept` | An executive summary of the activities required to transition from definition to active delivery. |\r\n| [[Plan Delivery]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the capability to construct detailed stage plans, tranche plans, and work package breakdowns. |\r\n| [[Solutions Development]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Solutions development is the function that determines the best way of satisfying the baselined require |\r\n| [[What does Control Mean]] | `Concept` | Exploration of the philosophy, principles, and practice of managerial control in P3M. |\r\n| [[Work Within A Team]] | `Competency` | Demonstrates the ability to collaborate effectively, communicate openly, and contribute productively as a member of a mu | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
