      "summary": "> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**:  > **Section**: \r\n> **Pillar**: Capability Maturity | **Type**: `maturity`\r\n\r\n Maturity Levels 4 And 5\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMAR",
      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Maturity Levels]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Capability Maturity | **Type**: `maturity`\r\n\r\n# Maturity Levels 4 And 5\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Characteristics and criteria for organizations operating at Quantitatively Managed (Level 4) and Optimizing (Level 5) maturity.\r\n\r\n## Maturity Level 4: Quantitatively Managed\r\nAt Level 4, project and programme processes are measured and controlled using statistical and quantitative techniques:\r\n- Quantitative objectives for quality and process performance are established.\r\n- Sub-processes are chosen that significantly contribute to overall process performance.\r\n- Process predictability is quantitatively understood.\r\n\r\n## Maturity Level 5: Optimizing\r\nAt Level 5, the organization continually improves its processes based on a quantitative understanding of business objectives and performance needs:\r\n- Focuses on continuous process improvement through incremental and innovative technological changes.\r\n- Root causes of common variations are identified and addressed systematically.\r\n- Knowledge sharing is institutionalized enterprise-wide.\r\n\r\n## Links\r\nSee [[Maturity Level 4 & 5]], [[Capability Maturity]], and [[Maturity Level 2 & 3]].\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Maturity Levels Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Maturity Level 4 & 5]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Resource Management Capability Maturity]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
