      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Knowledge | **Section**: `General Principles`\r\n\r\n# General Principles\r\n\r\n> [!ABSTRACT] Section Overview\r\n> Ethics, organizational design principles, and behavioral baselines for professional P3 practice.\r\n\r\n## Notes in this Section (2)\r\n\r\n| Note | Type | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| [[Ethics]] | `Concept` | - **Definition**: Ethics are the moral principles that govern someone’s behaviour or the way they perform an activity. |\r\n| [[General Principles of Organisation Management]] | `Guide` | - **Definition**: Organisation management is concerned with creating and maintaining a management structure that is appl | ---\r\n## Cross-Pillar Relationships\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Return to Master MOC]]\r\n- [[03. Processes/00 - Overview|Life Cycle Processes]]\r\n- [[06. Documentation & Artefacts/00 - Overview|Artefacts & Documentation]]\r\n- [[05. Competencies & Skills/00 - Overview|Competencies & Skills]]\r\n- [[09. Maturity Models/00 - Overview|Capability Maturity]]\r\n"
