      "body": "\r\n> [!NAV] Navigation\r\n> **Vault**: [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Overview]] > **Section**: [[00 - Overview|Financial Management]]\r\n> **Pillar**: Competence | **Type**: `competency`\r\n\r\n# Manage Funding Competency\r\n\r\n> [!SUMMARY] Overview\r\n> Demonstrates the capability to secure, release, and reconcile capital and operational funding across stage gateways.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nThe **Manage Funding** competency covers obtaining financial tranches from internal sponsors or external investors and managing cash flow liquidity throughout delivery.\r\n\r\n## Performance Criteria\r\n1. Identify funding sources, constraints, and release conditions.\r\n2. Prepare cash-flow draw-down schedules aligned with stage boundaries.\r\n3. Reconcile funding disbursements against verified project expenditures.\r\n4. Secure supplementary funding or return surplus funds at project close.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Navigation & Related Notes\r\n- **Up**: [[00 - Overview|Financial Management Overview]]\r\n- **Previous**: [[Manage Benefits]]\r\n- **Next**: [[Procurement Overall Goal]]\r\n\r\n### Related Concepts & Artefacts\r\n- [[00 - Praxis Framework Overview|Praxis Framework Master MOC]]\r\n- [[Capability Maturity]]\r\n- [[Complexity]]\r\n"
